    "text": "<p>Two Zener diodes (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>) having breakdown voltages of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively, are connected as shown in the circuit below. The output voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> variation with input voltage linearly increasing with time, is given by (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>)</p><p></p>"
  },
