  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>At time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;voltage across the first zener diode is increases linearly till it reaches&nbsp;it&#39;s breakdown voltage of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, after that voltage increases linearly till it reaches the breakdown voltage of second zener diode,</p><p>As soon as voltage across the zener diode reaches the breakdown voltage of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;of second zener diode, volatge becomes constant and doesn&#39;t change with time.</p>"
